{"problem": "weave_last\n\nThread value through a sequence of functions/forms\n\n>>> def double(x): return 2*x\n>>> def inc(x):    return x + 1\n>>> weave_last(1, inc, double)\n4\n\nIf the function expects more than one input you can specify those inputs\nin a tuple.  The value is used as the final input.\n\n>>> def add(x, y): return x + y\n>>> def pow(x, y): return x**y\n>>> weave_last(1, (add, 4), (pow, 2))  # pow(2, add(4, 1))\n32\n\nSo in general\n    weave_last(x, f, (g, y, z))\nexpands to\n    g(y, z, f(x))\n\n>>> def iseven(x):\n...     return x % 2 == 0\n>>> list(weave_last([1, 2, 3], (map, inc), (filter, iseven)))\n[2, 4]\n\nSee Also:\n    weave_first", "resolution": "def weave_last(val, *forms):\n    \"\"\" Thread value through a sequence of functions/forms\n\n    >>> def double(x): return 2*x\n    >>> def inc(x):    return x + 1\n    >>> weave_last(1, inc, double)\n    4\n\n    If the function expects more than one input you can specify those inputs\n    in a tuple.  The value is used as the final input.\n\n    >>> def add(x, y): return x + y\n    >>> def pow(x, y): return x**y\n    >>> weave_last(1, (add, 4), (pow, 2))  # pow(2, add(4, 1))\n    32\n\n    So in general\n        weave_last(x, f, (g, y, z))\n    expands to\n        g(y, z, f(x))\n\n    >>> def iseven(x):\n    ...     return x % 2 == 0\n    >>> list(weave_last([1, 2, 3], (map, inc), (filter, iseven)))\n    [2, 4]\n\n    See Also:\n        weave_first\n    \"\"\"\n    def evalform_back(val, form):\n        if callable(form):\n            return form(val)\n        if isinstance(form, tuple):\n            func, args = form[0], form[1:]\n            args = args + (val,)\n            return func(*args)\n    return reduce(evalform_back, forms, val)\n", "text": "weave_last"}